text:
sam: Quick note 1: we've seen multiple customer bundles include `undici` unexpectedly. Causes large ESM bundles and breakage in edge deploys. Want a small change in the SDK so undici is never a top-level import.

rachel: Agreed. Key idea: lazy-load / dynamic import at runtime only when global fetch is missing. That avoids static bundlers pulling it in.

tyler: Yea. Also recommend making `undici` an optional peerDependency/devDependency - not a hard dependency. Document the fallback clearly.

nisha: Minor TS thing: many users forget `lib.dom` and TS errors show up. We should add an example tsconfig in quickstart and a short troubleshooting section.

sam: Proposed helper (sync-ish for CJS + dynamic for ESM):
```ts
// utils/runtime-fetch.ts
export async function detectFetch(): Promise<typeof fetch> {
  if ((globalThis as any).fetch) return globalThis.fetch;
  // prefer dynamic import so bundlers don't include undici
  try {
    const m = await import('undici');
    return (m as any).fetch;
  } catch (e) {
    // fallback to require for older CJS environments
    try {
      // eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-var-requires
      const r = require('undici');
      return r.fetch;
    } catch (e2) {
      throw new Error('No fetch available: install undici (npm i undici) or run on a runtime with fetch');
    }
  }
}
```

rachel: Love it. Docs note: show a tiny wrapper the SDK uses internally and then how to override with `clientOptions.fetch` if someone needs a custom fetch.

tyler: Also list tested runtimes: Node 18, Node 20, Next.js (edge & server), Vercel Edge, Cloudflare, Bun (experimental). We should add matrix entries to CI.

nisha: TS example for docs: add `tsconfig.json` snippet recommending libs:
```json
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["es2021", "dom"],
    "target": "es2021"
  }
}
```

sam: Packaging note: keep conditional exports so both ESM and CJS work. Also ensure types are emitted and `types` field points to the d.ts entry.

ci-bot: CI #2420: packaging tests ran on Node 18/20 and ESM/CJS smoke.

rachel: Edge gotcha: AbortSignal and stream semantics differ. Add a short bullet: "Do not reuse AbortSignal across retries; prefer creating a fresh signal per request."

tyler: For sample apps, create three tiny samples: nextjs-server, nextjs-edge, node-serverless. Each shows optional `npm i undici` and how to set tsconfig.

sam: Action items: (1) add runtime-fetch helper in SDK (no top-level undici import), (2) update quickstart/sample-apps, (3) add tsconfig troubleshooting section, (4) add CI runtimes to matrix. I'll open the PR and tag reviewers.

